@startuml sequence-photo-log
' Menu Macro Fitter -- log a meal from a photo (issue #122)
' From backend/src/routes/photoAnalyses.js, controllers/photoAnalyses.js, integrations/claudeVision.js
' and docs/api-contract.md "Photo analysis" / "Meal logs". The student is already logged in.

skinparam defaultFontName Verdana
scale 2
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #999999
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9A227
autonumber

title Log a Meal From a Photo

participant "Client\n(web / mobile)" as Client
participant API
database MongoDB
participant "Claude Haiku 5.5\n(Anthropic)" as Claude

== Analyze the photo ==
Client -> API : POST /api/photo-analyses\n{ imageBase64, mediaType } + Bearer JWT
alt no or bad JWT
  API --> Client : 401
else body over 3 MiB, or over 3,000,000 chars
  API --> Client : 413 "Image too large"
else bad mediaType or base64
  API --> Client : 400
else no API key on the server
  API --> Client : 503 "Photo analysis unavailable"
else 20 analyses today (UTC)
  API --> Client : 429 "Daily photo limit reached"
end
API -> MongoDB : read all menu items\n(id, chain, name, macros)
API -> Claude : image + system prompt (rules + menu, cached)\noutput: JSON schema of items
alt request fails, refusal or max_tokens
  API --> Client : 502 "Photo analysis failed"
  note right of Client : a failed call does not\nuse up a daily slot
else model answered
  Claude --> API : { items: [ menuItemId?, name, servings,\ncalories, macros, confidence ] }
end
API -> API : DB trust: keep at most 10 items;\nmenuItemId not in MongoDB -> unmatched (null);\nmatched -> name, chain, macros from MongoDB;\nclamp servings 0.25-10, calories 0-5000, macros >= 0
API --> Client : 200 { items: PhotoItem[] }
note right of Client : nothing is saved;\nthe image is never stored

== Confirm and log ==
Client -> Client : confirm / edit screen\n(matched items: servings only)
Client -> API : POST /api/meal-logs (contract endpoint)\n{ entries: [ ..., source: "photo" ] } + Bearer JWT
API -> MongoDB : insert meal logs
API --> Client : 201 { entries: MealLog[] }

@enduml
